{
  "area": "routine-interruption",
  "description": "A routine’s whole lifecycle as an ordered script — assigned, adopted, preempted, released and picked back up — pinning the fact delta each step writes, whose plan it invalidated, and that resumption adopts the block due THEN rather than replaying the one that was interrupted. US-1 of 125-npc-routines-and-locomotion.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a-day-preempted-at-five-resumes-into-the-block-due-at-seven",
      "note": "THE case of this file, and the whole of what “resumes coherently” means. The smith is at the forge at five, a fight preempts it, and by the time the fight is over it is seven — so the day it picks back up is SUPPER, not the shift it was dragged out of. An implementation that queued the interrupted goal reproduces every fact here except the last two.",
